<title>USA: Olympus Real Estate buys Florida properties.</title>
<headline>Olympus Real Estate buys Florida properties.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olympus Real Estate Corp and its partner Ceebraid-Signal Corp said Tuesday they acquired four apartment properties in Miami and Orlando, Fla., for about $24 million.</p>
<p>Olympus was formed in May 1994 by private investment firm Hicks, Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Inc and investor David Deniger. Since its formation, the firm did more than $900 million in real estate investments in nine states.</p>
<p>Ceebraid owns and manages more than 12,000 apartment units in the U.S. Southeast and Northeast.</p>
</text>
